Z||000000||fieroshop||04-16-2000||12:45 AM||||Well after four months of not drivimg my 88 GT a I finally got it running again. All I had to do was replace all four brake rotors, crosover exhaust pipe, new flywheel, new clutch, clutch slave and master cylinders and finally a new clutch pedal. I had to turn down several jobs but I needed to get my pride and joy up and running. Oh yea almost forgot, while at the wrecking yard picking up a cylinder head for one of my jobs I found a cd radio out of a 92 Pontiac and installed it while we workr=ed on my car. Boy! does it sound sweet, I was able to hook up my sub-woofer at the same time. Speaking of sub=woofers, some at one point asked how to install a radio and get the sub-woofer to work. Since the Fieros do not have electric antenna's you simply use the antenn output from the radio to power your sub.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Homicidal||04-16-2000||12:16 PM||||Are we talking factory subs?  Because I just hooked up a 10" Polk Audio and it takes quite more power than that to run a sub!||||reg||1
